        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87750369?u=ccc1f52005708ae16bcb50e325e02145bff0ef7d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #41422.\">fix</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3491369017\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41422\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/41422/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41422\">#41422</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The word \"guarantee\" gives false hope that the returned color will always produce legible text. Let us elaborate more on the actual expected contrast and its limitations.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41445",
            "title": "Reword the 4.5:1 contrast and it's limitation related stuff",
            "date_modified": "2025-10-09T04:43:17.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-10-09T04:41:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "OnkarRuikar",
                "url": "https://github.com/OnkarRuikar"
            }
