            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome/Edge desktop 141 add support for the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/MediaDevices/getDisplayMedia\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">getDisplayMedia()</code></a> <code class=\"notranslate\">windowAudio</code> option. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5072779506089984\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5072779506089984</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a mention of it in the documentation. Note that in testing, the <code class=\"notranslate\">window</code> value didn't seem to work. See also the compat data PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3496008044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28130\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28130/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28130\">mdn/browser-compat-data#28130</a></p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
